# Axios / HTTP

## Do

- Use the shared Axios instance exported as **`api`** from **`src/libs/axios/instance.ts`** for app HTTP traffic.
- Keep **auth**, **global errors**, and **dev-only logging** in **`src/libs/axios/interceptors/**`**.
- Implement remote endpoints as **small typed functions** in **`src/services/**`** (e.g. future REST beside IndexedDB docs).
- Base URL: **`process.env['NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL']`** (optional when backend exists); document placeholders in **`.env.example`** when you add one.

## Don't

- Don’t create a **second `axios.create()`** for normal app calls.
- Don’t call **`axios` directly from `src/app/**` page files** — go through services (+ Query hooks when applicable).
- Don’t log full request/response bodies in interceptors (tokens / PII).

## Local docs note

- **`src/services/api/docs.service.ts`** uses **IndexedDB**, not Axios — keep that separation clear when adding HTTP services alongside.

## Security

- Follow **`000-core.mdc`**.
